# Line endings are checked out identically on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. The CI matrix includes Windows deliberately, and several selftests
# assert on the BYTES of tracked files: the control-character scan walks every tracked *.ts
# and *.md, and rules/java.md is parsed by pattern to check that each rule still carries a
# bad snippet, a good snippet and a why. With git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) the
# runner checks those same files out with CRLF, so ```java\n// bad stopped matching and the
# assertions reported "0 bad, 0 good" about a file nobody had touched.
#
# A checkout whose bytes depend on the platform makes every byte-level assertion
# platform-dependent, which is a trap rather than a feature. One rule, stated once.
* text=auto eol=lf
